// A dotted `::` head is namespaced, as an element's name is: `::catasto.upstream(...)` is the
// attribute `upstream` of the vocabulary `catasto`, `::c.upstream(...)` the same attribute under the
// alias `::use` gives it, and `::std.kind(...)` is `::kind(...)` written out.

::std.kind(fixture)
::use(catasto, as: c)
::c.upstream(commonfiles)
::std.meta(title: "Namespaced declarations")

A body, so the header is a header.
